## Chunk 5 design

### EffortProfile::tree_learn_seeds_for(effort)
  e0..=9 → 1 (unchanged; libjxl single-seed)
  e10   → 2 (unchanged)
  e11   → 8 (was 4 — chunk 5 expansion)

### Seed-slot split
For seed >= 4 in `tree_learn_seeds`:
  derive_seeded_sample_fraction(seed):
    seeds 0..=3 → None             (chunk-3-only slots)
    seed 4      → Some(0.40)
    seed 5      → Some(0.60)
    seed 6      → Some(0.70)
    seed 7      → None             (canonical; pairs with perm #3)
  derive_seeded_predictor_order(seed):
    seeds 0..=3 → canonical CANDIDATE_PREDICTORS  (chunk-3-only slots)
    seed 4      → perm[0] (canonical)
    seed 5      → perm[1] (strong-first)
    seed 6      → perm[2] (directional-first)
    seed 7      → perm[3] (full-reverse)

Chunk-3 perturbations (`derive_seeded_params`, `derive_seeded_stride`)
remain active for ALL seeds — they already cycle by `seed % 4` so seeds
4..7 layer chunk-4 dimensions on top of the same chunk-3 perturbation
pattern as seeds 0..3.

### Expectation
- e9:  byte-identical to chunk 4 / chunk 3 / chunk 2 / pre-RFC#45-chunk-2.
- e10: ≤ chunk 4 (still 2 seeds, both reserved for chunk-3-only
  perturbations because seeds < 4 ⇒ chunk-4 helpers no-op; bytes can
  differ from chunk 4 because chunk 4's seed 1 used Some(0.40) +
  perm[1], whereas chunk 5's seed 1 is chunk-3-only).
- e11: strictly ≥ chunk 3's wins by construction; should match or beat
  chunk 4.

